  "verbalization": "Zuclomiphene appears to exert its biological effects through a series of interconnected pathways that ultimately target Neuropilin-2. The evidence suggests that Zuclomiphene acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of both Arundinol B and Phomalide. These compounds, in turn, have targets that lead to Neuropilin-2. This chain of targets implies that Zuclomiphene may influence Neuropilin-2 through a series of intermediate molecules, potentially modulating cellular processes that involve Neuropilin-2. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, though indirect, relationship between Zuclomiphene and Neuropilin-2, likely mediated through multiple molecular intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the biological network in which Zuclomiphene operates, emphasizing the role of SNU-387 and its downstream targets in the overall mechanism of action.",
